# Patterns here deliberately carry NO trailing slash.
#
# `node_modules/` matches a DIRECTORY only, so a SYMLINK named node_modules is
# not ignored by it. That is how `node_modules -> /Users/conrad/dev/poly-styrene/node_modules`
# came to be committed and pushed to a public repo: an absolute path from one
# machine, which every clone then resolves to something that does not exist, and
# which on THAT machine points npm at another working tree's dependencies.
# Without the slash the pattern matches a file, a directory and a symlink alike.
node_modules
.wrangler
.dev.vars
worker-configuration.d.ts
coverage
dist
*.local.json
.DS_Store
